<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akropong</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akropong is a town on the Akuapem ridge in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> and the seat of the Okuapehene, paramount chief of the Akuapem state, since the 18th century. The Basel Mission settled there in 1835, and its seminary, founded in 1848, made the town a leading centre of education and of the Presbyterian Church in Ghana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akropong.jpg" alt="Akropong" width="104" height="101" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: West Akim Municipal District (AND) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akuapim_North_District_logo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
